  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-11-02 on dev ae02786fca (WI-jomik acceptance sweep, after PR #2004: shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates; PR #2006: a Rust method call never binds a free function). VERDICT: STILL_REPRODUCES. Repro run: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_C/hahud/fx/urls.py (copy of p4_review links1/fx_hahud: def index, class LoginView(View), Admin.index, Outer.LoginView, path(’’, index), path(’login/’, LoginView.as_view())); hypergumbo survey. Observed: usage_context for path(’login/’) symbol_ref python:urls.py:19-20:LoginView:class (nested Outer.LoginView; wrong). Control: path(’’) symbol_ref python:urls.py:5-6:index:function (right). dispatches_to ANY /login/ -> urls.py:9-10:LoginView:class (right, 0.5, disambiguation_fallback True). Note: Only the nested-class half remains, as the item’s 2026-11-01 review says. The method-vs-function half shows correct output. New since review: the dispatches_to edges now carry disambiguation_fallback True at 0.5. Fixtures: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_*/."  # a28a
